SUMMARY:Lakefest — Bluegrass + Higher Vibrations
LOCATION:Ski Beach Park / Swim Beach — 41216 Park Ave\, Big Bear Lake\, C
 A 92315
DESCRIPTION:Lakefest’s full Saturday moves from bluegrass and Americana i
 nto a short punk/post-hardcore set\, BMX\, a drum circle and a still-unann
 ounced 7 PM finale. The current registration schedule is newer than the to
 urism page and is used here.\n\nWHEN\nSat\, Aug 29\, 2026\, 11:00 AM–8:0
 0 PM\n\nPRICE / ADMISSION\n• Free general admission\; the registration p
 age offers a $0 general-admission ticket\n• Paint & Sip: $41.87 per sess
 ion including the listed fee\; includes supplies\, two adult beverages and
  charcuterie\n• Food and other drinks are sold separately\n\nSCHEDULE\n
 • 11:00 AM — beer garden\, food vendors\, kids zone and yard games ope
 n\n• 12:00 PM — Paint & Sip session\n• 12:00–1:30 PM — Honey Buc
 kets\n• 1:30 PM — open mic\n• 2:00–3:30 PM — The Guesthouse Band
 \n• 2:30 PM — Paint & Sip session\n• 3:30 PM — Puma Karate demonst
 ration\n• 4:00–5:30 PM — Rose’s Pawn Shop\n• 5:30–6:00 PM — 
 drum circle\n• 6:15–6:45 PM — Dog’s Breakfast\n• 6:45–7:00 PM 
 — BMX show\n• 7:00–8:00 PM — act still TBD\n\nWHAT TO EXPECT\n• 
 Honey Buckets is a Southern California single-mic bluegrass band with a he
 avy-metal streak\n• The Guesthouse mixes bluegrass with modern/pop influ
 ences\, close harmonies and fast rhythms\n• Rose’s Pawn Shop plays mod
 ern American roots music spanning bluegrass\, punky tempos\, rock\, folk a
 nd country\n• Dog’s Breakfast is Inland Empire punk/post-hardcore/emo/
 indie rock\n• The festival also advertises a beer garden\, food vendors/
 trucks\, kids activities\, yard games\, local art and a vendor village\n\n
 USEFUL NOTES\n• Visit Big Bear says there is no on-site parking\; consid
 er the free trolley or bike valet\n• A satellite lot is advertised near 
 Fox Farm Road and Garstin Drive\, but the shuttle-day wording is contradic
 tory\; verify before relying on it\n• This is a genuine either/or choice
  after 5:30 PM: Lakefest’s Higher Vibrations block overlaps the free Nic
 k Waterhouse + McCharmlys concert in The Village\n\nTBD / VERIFY BEFORE GO
 ING\n• The 7:00–8:00 PM finale remains unannounced\n• Visit Big Bear
  still shows an older Community and Kids Stage schedule and labels the eve
 ning Punk in the Back with three TBD slots\; the newer registration page i
 nstead says Higher Vibrations and identifies all but the 7 PM act\n• Sat
 ellite parking/shuttle operating days need confirmation\n\nCONFLICTS / SAM
 E-DAY OPTIONS\n• Overlaps or competes with: Summer Concert Series — Ni
 ck Waterhouse + The McCharmlys (Sat\, Aug 29\, 2026\, 5:30 PM–8:30 PM).\
 n\nOFFICIAL SOURCES\n• Current registration and schedule: https://runsig
 nup.com/TicketEvent/BigBearsLakefest\n• Visit Big Bear schedule and logi
 stics: https://www.bigbear.com/events/lakefest-big-bear-lake/\n• Honey B
 uckets: https://honeybuckets.band/\n• The Guesthouse Band: https://www.g
 uesthousetheband.com/\n• Rose’s Pawn Shop: https://rosespawnshop.com/a
 bout/\n• Dog’s Breakfast: https://dogsbreakfastie.bandcamp.com/album/h
 ow-will-i-run-the-show\n\nCALENDAR STATUS: DETAILS_TBD\nLast checked: 2026
 -08-09\nDetails can change. Recheck the official source before making a sp
 ecial trip.
