  Lake\, CA 92315
DESCRIPTION:Opening day for Big Bear’s long-running German festival: four
  bands across indoor/outdoor stages\, German food and beer\, stein-holding
  and log-sawing contests\, mechanical bull\, games\, vendors and a Kids Zo
 ne.\n\nWHEN\nSat\, Sep 12\, 2026\, 1:00 PM–11:00 PM\n\nPRICE / ADMISSION
 \n• Advance adult age 13–61: $28.68 with fee\n• Senior age 62+: $19.
 10\n• Child age 3–12: $10.58\; age 2 and under free\n• Preferred ind
 oor/outdoor seating: $73.41\n\nSCHEDULE\n• 1:00 PM — gates\, Midway/Ki
 ds Zone and vendors open\n• 1:30 PM — Ladyhosen Band indoors\; DragonW
 olfe outdoors\n• 6:00 PM — Die Sauerkrauts indoors\; Mary Dyer Band ou
 tdoors\n• 10:00 PM — Midway/Kids Zone and vendors close\n• 11:00 PM 
 — festival closes\n\nWHAT TO EXPECT\n• Saturday entry slots are 1:00
 –4:00\, 4:00–7:00 or After Dark from 7:30\; guests may stay until clos
 ing after entry\n• Traditional food/beer\, contests\, mechanical bull\, 
 arts/crafts and inflatables\n• Rain or shine\; photo ID\; no re-entry or
  outside food/drink\; service animals only\; alcohol 21+\n\nUSEFUL NOTES\n
